{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"9":{"eng-name":"Zakat (Kitab Al-Zakat)","ara-name":"كتاب الزكاة"}},"section_detail":{"9":{"hadithnumber_first":1556,"hadithnumber_last":1700,"arabicnumber_first":1556,"arabicnumber_last":1700}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":1646,"arabicnumber":1646,"text":"Rapporté par Ibn al-Firasi رضي الله عنه : Al-Firasi a demandé au Messager d’Allah ﷺ : « Puis-je mendier, Messager d’Allah ? » Le Prophète ﷺ a dit : « Non, mais si tu n’as vraiment pas d’autre choix, demande à des gens honnêtes. »","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}],"reference":{"book":9,"hadith":91},"chapter":{"id":29,"ara-name":"باب فِي الاِسْتِعْفَافِ","eng-name":"On Abstinence From Begging","isFirstHadith":false}}]}